body.en:
Decide on **data volume, update frequency, freshness requirement, where compute should run and team skills**:
- low volume + must be instant → trigger (ideally mark-and-process);
- moderate volume, minutes of lag OK, T-SQL team → Change Tracking job;
- .NET team, scale-out, near real time → Functions SQL trigger;
- low-code, business workflow → Logic Apps;
- high volume with history → CDC;
- many consumers, event-driven architecture → CES.
**Deletes**: cascade-delete chunk/embedding rows (`ON DELETE CASCADE`) or handle delete operations in your processor. **Model changes**: re-embed every row (track `ModelVersion`), switch queries when done, and **drop and recreate the vector index** after a near-complete replacement so it fits the new data distribution.
